    "ThermalFlowScreen": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "The heat load read against the Ohio daily-maximum criterion at one design low flow.\n\nThe direct heat analog of :class:`watermark.hydrology.toxics.CriterionScreen`.\n``thermal_capacity_mw`` = ``rho*cp*Q*(daily_max - ambient)`` is the loading capacity;\n``exceedance_factor`` = ``reject_heat / thermal_capacity`` (>= 1 exceeds). When the design\nflow is 0 (the Ottawa 1Q10) or the ambient already meets the criterion, the capacity is 0 and\nboth the factor and the mixed temperature are ``None`` (not ``Inf``) — ``flag`` is\n``no_capacity``. ``capacity_fraction`` = ``thermal_capacity / reject_heat`` is the\npartition-robustness metric: the fraction of the condenser rejection that would exhaust the\nreach's entire thermal capacity.",
      "properties": {
        "flow_label": {
          "title": "Flow Label",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "design_flow": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ProvenancedValue"
        },
        "thermal_capacity_mw": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Thermal Capacity Mw"
        },
        "delta_t_c": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/ProvenancedValue"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        },
        "mixed_c": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/ProvenancedValue"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        },
        "exceedance_factor": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Exceedance Factor"
        },
        "capacity_fraction": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Capacity Fraction"
        },
        "headroom_fraction": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Headroom Fraction"
        },
        "mixed_over_criterion": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Mixed Over Criterion"
        },
        "flag": {
          "title": "Flag",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "note": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Note"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "flow_label",
        "design_flow",
        "thermal_capacity_mw",
        "delta_t_c",
        "mixed_c",
        "exceedance_factor",
        "capacity_fraction",
        "flag"
      ],
      "title": "ThermalFlowScreen",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ThermalScenario": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "One cooling archetype's in-stream heat load, screened at the reach's design low flows.\n\nThe Phase-2 screen carried a single conservative bound (the whole condenser rejection reaching\nthe water). A scenario makes the **heat partition** explicit instead: ``instream_heat_mw`` is\nwhat actually enters the stream under this archetype, and ``instream_fraction`` is its share of\nthe condenser rejection. The point of running all three is that they span two orders of\nmagnitude of partition and *all* exceed the reach's capacity — the robustness claim, quantified.",
      "properties": {
        "scenario": {
          "title": "Scenario",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "basis": {
          "title": "Basis",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "reject_heat_mw": {
